  <section id="work" class="home-section narrative">
    <h2>Work & background</h2>
    <p>At <a href="https://www.meritholdings.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Merit</a>, we acquire, operate, and build vertical software businesses with a long-term ownership horizon.</p>
    <p>Before Merit, I helped build <strong>Dispatch</strong> in field services, worked in growth investing at <strong>OpenView</strong> across Series A, Series B, and later stages, and invested at <strong>Pathlight Ventures</strong> from inception and pre-seed through early Series A.</p>
    <p>That work has spanned fundraising, corporate development, early-stage and growth investing, and company building from both a product and go-to-market perspective. Mostly vertical software, across B2B and consumer.</p>
    <p>I also previously founded <a href="https://www.racepace.cc/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Racepace</a>, an AI cycling coach that brings training history and day-to-day conversation together to help athletes plan, adapt, and improve.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section narrative">
    <h2>Questions I keep coming back to</h2>
    <p>What makes a software business defensible? How does value delivered to customers become lasting equity value? And how do product, distribution, and capital allocation reinforce one another?</p>
    <p>I’m interested in what actually makes a business more valuable over time: its economics, competitive position, and ability to keep serving customers well.</p>
  </section>

